gnome-shell-extension-incus-monitor (1.0.0~rc.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial commit
  * feat(core): add Result type and IncusError union
  * chore: ignore Python bytecode; record review contracts in roadmap
  * feat(http): add strict incremental HTTP/1.1 codec
  * feat(incus): decode and validate response envelopes
  * feat(incus): decode server and instance models
  * docs(roadmap): record review contracts for T08-T11
  * feat(core): discover the Incus socket with cancellation
  * feat(core): compute metrics and format readouts
  * feat(incus): add Incus client over a transport port
  * feat(incus): gate on required API extensions
  * docs(roadmap): record T09-T12 contracts from T05-T08 reviews
  * feat(core): add the polling monitor with actions and back-off
  * feat(adapters): add Gio transport, clock, settings, probe and launcher
  * feat(core): present snapshots as a view model
  * feat(prefs): add the Adw preferences window
  * feat(ui): add the panel indicator, menu and composition root
  * feat(i18n): add the translation template and Spanish catalogue
  * fix(adapters): write requests with GLib.Bytes.new so GNOME 46 can reach
    Incus
  * test(contract): record Incus 7.0.1 fixtures and run client tests on both
    series
  * fix(core): treat a CPU usage of -1 as unavailable instead of failing the
    whole list
  * feat(scripts): add demo instances and make the nested shell follow your
    appearance
  * feat(core): log the cause of a decode, api or timeout failure once per
    episode
  * fix(ui): keep detail rows readable by not styling them as insensitive
  * feat(ui): add room before the copy button and a separator before Open
    Shell
  * feat(ui): separate Open Shell from the lifecycle buttons
  * fix(ui): align the rules and inset the Open Shell highlight in the
    expanded row
  * feat(scripts): add a headless screenshot harness and skills for verifying
    the extension live
  * fix(ui): show only the IPv4 address and keep rows in place while the menu
    is open
  * fix(ui): release the highlight of the row header and Open Shell when the
    pointer leaves
  * fix(ui): keep keyboard focus on the row while an action runs and return it
    afterwards
  * fix(scripts): start a stopped test VM, drop a stale per-user copy and set
    a login password
  * fix(ui): stop Open Shell from taking focus when an action settles and keep
    the address row height
  * fix(scripts): remove the previous package from the test VM before pushing
    the new one
  * feat(ui): group the expanded row in a faint panel so the next instance
    stands apart
  * feat(scripts): reuse the desktop VM without rebooting and give it the
    host's demo instances
  * docs(roadmap): record the post-1.0 backlog
  * docs(roadmap): mark the manual matrix ready for review

